Big - O

condition  :-
  f(n) = c + g(n) for all n >= n.


Big - Theta

condition:-
  f(n) = c*g(n) for all n>=n.


TREE:-

Degree of Node = number of children of the node.
Depth of Node = Number of edges from root to the node.
Level of node = depth,under our zero based indexing, level of root node = 0.
Height of node = Number of edges from the node to the deepest leaf node.
height of tree = height of root node.
subtree = tree formed by a node and all its descendents.


Properties of binary tree:-

1.maximum number of nodes at level l = 2^l;
example:-
level 0 = 2^0 = 1;
level 1 = 2^1 = 2;
level 2 = 2^2 = 4;
Q. maximum number of nodes at level 10
A. 2^10 = 1024

2.maximum number of nodes in a binary tree of height h = 2^(h+1) - 1
example:-
height 0 = 2^(0+1) - 1 = 1
height 1 = 2^(1+1) - 1 = 3
height 2 = 2^(2+1) - 1 = 7
Q. maximum number of nodes in a binary tree of height 10?
A. 2^(10+1) - 1 = 2047

3.Minimum number of nodes in a binary tree of height h = h+1
4.Miximum number of leaves in a binary tree of height h = 2^h
5.Full binary tree = a binary tree in which every node has either 0 or 2 children
6.Complete binary tree = a binary tree in which every level except possibly the last, is completely filled, and all nodes are as far left as possible

Properties of complete binary tree:-

1.Complete binary tree is soid to be proper binary tree where all leaves have the same depth or same level.
2.In a complete binary tree with a nodes, height of the tree is log(n)
3.All the leaves are completely filled except possibly the last level.
